    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0906" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg896"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office U. S. Military Telegraph</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">War Department, Washington, D.
                            C.,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Orders have been given for the arrest and punishment of the fabricators and
                    publishers of the spurious proclamation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        State.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">U. S. Minister Plenipotentiary, London,
                            England.</hi></p>
                    <p>[Copy to Hon. William L. Dayton, U. S. minister plenipotentiary, Paris.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
